Three Angles to Anywhere — Transit Map · Lemo-Opuscar

Picture
- Every line, tick, ring, label, plate, pin, lantern, train car, street, park and river is drawn in code (demo/network.js, demo/main.js). No generated or stock images.
- Halden, its five lines (Copper, Violet, Fern, Ring, Saffron) and all 36 station names are invented. Any resemblance to a real transit system, station or logo is accidental; none was used as a source for names, colours or layout.

Fonts (SIL Open Font License 1.1, licence file in demo/fonts/OFL.txt; the .ttf is not committed, build.sh downloads it)
- Barlow Medium — The Barlow Project Authors (jpt/barlow), via google/fonts
- Line numbers in roundels, arrows, ticks and check marks are drawn in code, not set in a font.

Voice
- Kokoro TTS v1.0 (hexgrad/Kokoro-82M, Apache-2.0), voice bf_emma, via kokoro-onnx
- Speech check only (not in the film): faster-whisper / OpenAI Whisper (MIT)

Music
- Original composition, synthesised in numpy (demo/mix.py): marimba and vibraphone (additive/FM), sine bass, detuned-saw pad, bells (FM), rail ticks and a muted kick. No samples.

Sound design
- Ruling-pen hiss, water, ticks, snaps, paper slides, felt thuds, door beeps, pneumatic hiss, wheel clacks and rumble are synthesised in numpy (demo/mix.py, core/audio/sfx.py). No recordings.
